# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Supabase project settings -> API.
#
# Newer Supabase projects issue a publishable key (sb_publishable_...);
# legacy projects issue an anon key. Either works - set whichever you have.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="sb_publishable_..."
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="legacy-anon-key"

# The FastAPI backend (control-panel/backend). Server-side only.
BACKEND_URL="http://127.0.0.1:8000"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- deployment
# On Vercel, set BACKEND_URL above to the hosted FastAPI service instead, e.g.
#   BACKEND_URL="https://supply-desk-api.onrender.com"     (no trailing slash)
# It is deliberately NOT prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_: the browser never calls the
# backend directly. Every call goes through /api/backend/*, which runs
# server-side, reads the session from cookies and forwards it as a bearer
# token - which is also what makes a plain download link work.

# One-time escape hatch, for a database where migration 0006 has not been run
# yet and therefore has no accounts at all. Without it the sign-in gate would
# strand you at a form nobody can satisfy. Remove it once 0006 has run.
# AUTH_SETUP_MODE=1
